./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3046:SHEET6.md:10:- **1c. RECON correction**: "no independent reproof of ≤5 exists" is WRONG. Sigray's thesis Theorem 9.1 proves td(f,g) ≥ 6 for any counterexample, independently of Żołądek, same year, different machinery (decorated Eggers–Wall trees vs Newton–Puiseux charts). Never journal-published (zbMATH lists only his monodromy + kp′q−lpq′ papers) but cited as the bound by Makar-Limanov (arXiv:2106.06869) and Borisov (arXiv:1901.04073: "current best lower bound ... is 6"). Caveats on BOTH proofs: Żołądek's neighboring gcd sections have a **documented gap** (GGV arXiv:1401.1784: Lemma 4.10 "claims without proof that I₂ ⊂ (1/m)Γ(f₂)"; his claimed B>33 fails, B≥16 stands only via GGV's independent reproof) — his topdeg-5 sections have no reported gap but are unaudited; Sigray's thesis is unrefereed. Also flagged: arXiv:2407.13795 (Moskowicz, 2024, 8pp) claims NO Keller map has prime field-extension degree — unpublished, treat as unvetted; if ever verified it would exclude 7 and make 6, 8, 9 the whole frontier.
./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3048:SHEET6.md:15:- **(B) Sigray's decorated Eggers–Wall trees** (verbatim, thesis in hand): Abhyankar normal form (§2: Newton polygons in rectangles, fibers with 2 points at infinity); Eggers–Wall tree of Puiseux expansions of f-fiber branches at infinity (§3); extended Abhyankar fundamental theorem + partial order (§4); td and pole orders of g computed from tree data (§5, Props 5.5/5.8); tree structure symbols ↘↗ (§6); finite critical values budget (§7, Cor 7.1); Jacobian-forced number theory linking neighboring vertices (§8, Prop 8.1); §9: decoration Q(F) = (D_F, deg p_F, ν_F, M_F, κ_F(1−π(F))) must propagate along the "characteristic sequence" F₀→…→(0,y) to the root, under Diophantine constraints, with budget Σλ_{F_i} ≤ td−2 (St 9.4) — and no admissible propagation survives for td ≤ 5.
./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3051:SHEET6.md:21:- **The real wall is at 9, not 6**: Sigray exhibits a decorated Eggers–Wall tree satisfying ALL his constraints at td = 9 with (deg f, deg g) = (48,64) — Moh's exceptional case — matching Orevkov's holomorphic "counterexamples to JC at infinity" (minimal td 9, bidegree (48,64); DO-I: the local-at-infinity method can at best reach ~8). Sigray verbatim: the problem at higher degree is not that computations are "more involved" but that a consistent tree EXISTS at 9. Corollary: td ∈ {6,7,8} is the entire remaining runway for at-infinity methods, with no known consistency obstruction below 9.
