   608	
   609	## 6. Consequence for `REDUCTION.md` T1–T10
   610	
   611	The exact new sequential arrow is
   612	
   613	\[
   614	\begin{aligned}
   615	 \mathrm{JC2\ false}
   616	 &\xRightarrow{\mathrm{T2}}
   617	 \text{one selected GGV-minimal standard polynomial pair with its native ledger}
   618	 \\
   619	 &\xRightarrow{\text{Theorems 2.1, 3.1 and (4.1)--(4.5)}}
   620	 \text{an explicit Sigray-normalized representative of the same pair,}\\
   621	 &\hspace{38mm}\text{same }td\text{, with the GGV ledger exactly recoverable.}
   622	\end{aligned}
   623	\tag{6.1}
   624	\]
   625	
   626	Thus the following become theorem-level statements.
   627	
   628	- **T2 \(\to\) enhanced T4, for the selected pair:** no independent
   629	  re-normalization is needed; the component-sorted pair
   630	  \(C\circ(P,Q)\) is orbitwise lex-minimal, and (3.1) gives its Sigray
   631	  frame.
   632	- **T2 plus native pre-Laurent T3 \(\to\) enhanced T4:** every
   633	  polynomial-native polygon corner, leading face, direction, and endpoint
   634	  is carried by (4.1)–(4.4).  Additional rational GGV5 chain
   635	  corners/directions and \((p_h,q_h)\) tags are retained losslessly as the
   636	  raw/recoverable valuation ledger (4.3)–(4.5), with oriented endpoints
   637	  separately recorded by (4.4).  This is not a claim that Laurent leading
   638	  forms live in the same polynomial chart, nor a claim of native
   639	  transposed-chain admissibility.  The fork drawn in T4 closes at the
   640	  normalization layer.
   641	- **Composition with T5–T7:** the same selected counterexample retains its
   642	  topological degree, so T5 applies and the existing Sigray tree/entry
   643	  constructions of T6–T7 can be attached without discarding the GGV
   644	  ledger.
   645	
   646	Nothing else is promoted by this theorem.
   647	
   648	| T-link | consequence of this document |
   649	|---|---|
   650	| T1 | unchanged; the literal starting condition remains false |
   651	| T2 | unchanged existential GGV theorem; now has a compatible T4 continuation |
   652	| T3 | existing published/preprint and bounded perimeters unchanged; native data transport is proved only before Laurent cuts |
   653	| T4 | strengthened for the T2-selected pair by Theorem 3.1; arbitrary-pair T4 remains the existing Sigray/Abhyankar theorem |
   654	| T5 | unchanged published lower bound \(td\ge6\) |
   655	| T6 | unchanged conditional sheet/tree perimeter; it now coexists with recoverable GGV data on the same equivalence class |
   656	| T7 | unchanged conditional mass/entry theorem; composable with (6.1) |
   657	| T8 | unchanged local marked-event landing perimeter |
   658	| T9 | unchanged sector-specific enumerations and conditionalities |
   659	| T10 | still **NOT ESTABLISHED** |
   660	
   661	In particular, this theorem does not prove full-configuration landing, a
   662	generic off-axis completeness theorem, or an upper bound on \(td\).
   663	
   664	## 7. Dependencies and evidence
   665	
   666	1. **GGV rectangle/selection input.** Guccione–Guccione–Valqui,
