   668	   Proposition 4.7, the standardization proposition, and Corollary 5.21;
   669	   see the [arXiv source](https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.1784) and the exact
   670	   campaign statement in [REDUCTION.md](REDUCTION.md) T2–T3.  The GGV
   671	   theorem is existential over all counterexamples.
   672	2. **New algebraic input.** Theorem 1.1 and Theorem 2.1 are proved here.
   673	   They use only elementary facts about a coordinate Hamiltonian LND, with
   674	   the filtered-leading and factorial-closure steps proved in the text.
   675	3. **Sigray nomenclature.** Notations 2.1–2.4 and Lemma 2.1's displayed
   676	   rectangle conditions in [refs/sigray_full.pdf](refs/sigray_full.pdf),
   677	   audited in [SIGRAY-AUDIT.md](SIGRAY-AUDIT.md).  Theorem 3.1 does not use
   678	   Sigray's Abhyankar-based existence proof for the selected GGV pair.
   679	4. **Admissible-chain fixture.** [lib/FAMILIES.md](lib/FAMILIES.md) and
   680	   `lib/families.py`, whose GGV5 completeness scope is bounded exactly as
   681	   recorded in [REDUCTION.md](REDUCTION.md).  This document transports a
