   218	## 5. Consequences
   219	
   220	### 5a. The book stays 8; the A3L1 kill route is closed
   221	
   222	The λ_root ≥ 1 lemma is DEAD as a kill: its content is empty on exactly
   223	the survivor set (case-IV terminals), by the survivors' own terminal
   224	hypothesis. SHEET6-CAMPAIGN header "next kills" should drop it; the
   225	counterexample template is instead STRENGTHENED (5b). No class dies; no
   226	class is resurrected; canonical book unchanged: td ≤ 5: 0; td = 6: 4
   227	single-pole r9/M2 + two-pole residue A (4 IV classes).
   228	
   229	### 5b. New forced rigidity (the ledger's positive product)
   230	
   231	For EVERY one of the 8 (LR2): the x-side of a carrier is a single
   232	Puiseux cluster — one cv vertex, κ_G = 1, no x-side splitting or
   233	characteristic exponent below height R ≥ 3. This is a new, checkable
   234	constraint feeding the coefficient-template lift (the campaign's other
   235	endgame thread): any candidate (f,g) must have its ENTIRE x-side Newton
   236	structure trivial to depth R.
   237	
   238	For the 4 slack-0 classes additionally (every ledger row exact):
   239	1. x-side: π_G = R exactly; both p- and g-patterns unsplit below R
   240	   (full slopes l_f, l_g the whole way);
   241	2. y-side: each priced orbit cluster carries exactly ONE cv vertex of
   242	   mass exactly its (24)-price (e.g. SP-2: κ_H = 1, π_H = 2, twice);
   243	   no further y-side cv vertex anywhere (pole clusters pure — forced;
   244	   orbit subtrees unsplit below their cv vertices);
   245	3. δ_a = 0 for EVERY a ∈ C: no fiber in the whole pencil may carry any
   246	   g-finite puncture with Λ(P) > κ_{F̂_P}(π(F̂_P)−1) — total
   247	   non-degeneracy of every direction family at every special value.
   248	
   249	### 5c. The surviving attack surfaces (precise, none printed)
   250	
   251	1. **δ-strictness at direction collisions.** The x-family's direction
   252	   polynomial has degree deg p_G = l_f ≥ 15 (single-pole) at the cv
   253	   vertex, so a* with mult(p_G − a*, c) ≥ 2 EXIST (critical values of a
   254	   nonconstant polynomial). Prop 7.3 proves Λ-mass ≥ κπ−κ with equality
   255	   iff mult = 1 but does NOT prove strictness at mult ≥ 2. A strict
   256	   version (one extra unit of δ at some collision fiber) would kill all
   257	   four slack-0 classes at once — this is the exact quantitative question
   258	   the ledger isolates. Genuinely new mathematics (a local excess formula
   259	   for Prop 7.4's δ); nothing in §7 decides it.
   260	2. **x-side realizability vs the templates.** LR2's single-cluster/κ=1/
   261	   unsplit-to-height-R x-side must coexist with the pinned y-side
   262	   patterns (AF3 §4 entry family; L1 §5 rigid merge template) inside one
   263	   polynomial pair of the given type. This is the same Puiseux-transport
   264	   tier as L1 §7(ii), now with BOTH ends of the tree pinned.
   265	3. **h₁-branch budget (unchanged, L1 §7(i))**: the (22)-ledger charges
   266	   only g-critical-value vertices; h₁-branches at non-p directions remain
   267	   outside every printed budget — confirmed here as a structural gap of
   268	   the counting frame, not closable by re-partitioning (22).
