   209	## 5. DS4 (the jump-cell menu factors through w)
   210	
   211	Let G be a merge with arriving all-μ=1 edges from last-segment vertices
   212	H_e, and let (dp_c, dq_c) be the merged reduced pattern (MP6(d) menu:
   213	IIa (rν, (r+l)ν+1); ZCH ((r−1)ν+1, (r−1+l)ν+1); I (r, r+l)),
   214	Δ_c := dq_c − dp_c.
   215	
   216	### 5a. The handshake
   217	
   218	For every μ_e = 1 edge governed by the case-(I)/(II) equations:
   219	
   220	    κ̄_G = (κ̄_e + n_e)/ν_e,   D_G/i := μ_e(ρ_e + n_e)/ν_e = (ρ_e + n_e)/ν_e
   221	    ⟹  **κ̄_G − D_G/i = (κ̄_e − ρ_e)/ν_e = w_e.**
   222	
   223	One line, cell-independent. Consequences: (i) the join condition (common
   224	(κ̄_G, D/i) across edges, SHEET6-MP-REVIEW §5c layer J) forces **all
   225	arriving chains to carry the same w**; (ii) solving the edge equation
   226	against the cell exactly as in §3 gives
   227	
   228	    κ̄_G = w·dq_c/Δ_c,   D_G/i = w·dp_c/Δ_c,   ρ_G = w/Δ_c,
   229	
   230	so the **entire merged-child datum depends only on (w, cell)** — not on
   231	the segment depth, not on (ν_e, n_e, κ̄_e) separately. (The per-edge
   232	admissibility n_e ∈ ℕ*, n_e ≡ −κ̄_e (mod ν_e) does depend on the state
   233	(w, ν_e, n_e); see §6 for why this does not spoil stabilization.)
