   246	Finitely many (family, ν, l, M = gcd) per (w, r ≤ m) — the SHEET6-MP-REVIEW
   247	§5a per-frame finiteness, now *uniform in depth*. Cascade cells (l = 0,
   248	M = 1 emission) are the infinite ν-family, but their child is again an
   249	M=1 segment entry with **w_child = w·(r+l)/(lν+1)** (= r·w at l = 0),
   250	ν-independent at l = 0; with MP1's Σ(r−1) = m−1 the composed closure
   251	multiplies at most m−1 such factors — still a finite computable w-set.
