    66	## 2. The td-uniform gcd pattern (question (a))
    67	
    68	The AF3 pin (SHEET6-AF3.md §1: Not 5.2 + Prop 5.1(i)/(iii) + Prop 4.2
    69	h0 = g + Not 8.1, pp. 19-44 — NOTHING in the chain uses td <= 6 or
    70	|T_a,pole| = 1) gives at every pole vertex
    71	    M_F = gcd(deg p_F, deg p_g,F) = gcd(b*alpha, b*beta) = **b**.
    72	So the gcd pattern of table (23) and its extension to every td is: **the
    73	entry M is the p-side multiplier b, full stop.** Kill (Prop 8.4, p. 44,
    74	needs T_a,pole singleton = single-pole hypothesis): b = 1 => excluded.
    75	
    76	Row-by-row at Lambda <= 6 this reproduces SHEET6-AF3 §2 exactly (rows
    77	1,2,3,5,6,7,10,11 have b=1: dead; rows 4,8,9 have b=2,3,2: live).
    78	
    79	**Prime td.** Let td = p prime. From (R3), a*b*(alpha/nu)*beta = p in case
    80	(A) resp. a*b*alpha*(beta/nu) = p in case (B), all factors in N*.
    81	- Case (B): alpha >= 2 divides the product, so alpha = p and
    82	  a = b = beta/nu = 1; then nu = beta > alpha = p and nu | b*alpha - 1 =
    83	  p - 1 < p < nu — IMPOSSIBLE. Case (B) contributes no row at all.
    84	- Case (A): beta >= 3 divides the product, so beta = p, a = b = 1,
    85	  alpha = nu, and the only condition left is nu = alpha | b*beta - 1 =
    86	  p - 1. Rows: {(alpha, p) : alpha | p-1, 2 <= alpha < p, nu = alpha,
    87	  a = b = 1}, each with (D,Dg) = (P,Pg) = (alpha,p), Lambda = p.
    88	  (Check td=7: (2,7),(3,7),(6,7) — precisely the campaign's Lambda=7 table
    89	  rows, SHEET6-CAMPAIGN §1.)
    90	All prime-td rows have b = 1, hence M = 1: **entry-dead**.
    91	
    92	**Composite td.** E(td) := {rows with b >= 2} is NONEMPTY for every
    93	composite td >= 4: write td = a*b*alpha with b, alpha >= 2 (possible iff
    94	td has a composite divisor iff td composite), take beta := b*alpha - 1
    95	and nu := beta (case (B): nu | beta, nu | b*alpha - 1 trivially;
    96	beta > alpha since alpha*(b-1) > 1; gcd(alpha,beta) = 1 since beta = -1
    97	mod alpha; beta >= 3). So entry-level exclusion is exactly the prime td's.
    98	
    99	**N1 refinement** (SHEET6-III, mod H5a): gcd(kap-bar, nu) = 1 at every
   100	nu >= 2 vertex. At the entry, kap-bar = a(alpha+beta) and (R2) gives
   101	alpha+beta == alpha (case B) resp. beta (case A) mod nu, both coprime to
   102	nu; hence **N1 at entry <=> gcd(a, nu) = 1**. (Reproduces the row-3 kill:
   103	a=2, nu=2.)
