   259	## 5. L1-IIa is locally FALSE: the l = 1 pattern exists and is rigid
   260	
   261	Reduced ODE at G_m in t = eta^nu (p = pt = (t-a_1)(t-a_2), q = eta pt s,
   262	s = t - b, rho = dp/dq = 2nu/(3nu+1)):
   263	
   264	    rho pt s + nu rho t pt s' + (rho - 1) nu t pt' s = c~,   c~ != 0.
   265	
   266	Top degree cancels precisely at rho = 2nu/(3nu+1) (consistent with
   267	Cor 6.1 = the merge ratio equations, dp/dq = 6/10 at nu = 3). The rest
   268	is a linear system with UNIQUE solution given the scale sigma := a_1 +
   269	a_2 != 0:
   270	
   271	    a_1 a_2 = sigma^2 (nu-1)/(4nu),    b = sigma (nu+1)/(2nu),
   272	    i.e.  a_{1,2} = (sigma/2)(1 ± nu^{-1/2}),
   273	
   274	all side conditions holding (roots distinct, nonzero, b not a root,
   275	c~ != 0) — verified exactly for nu = 3, 5, 7, 9 (l1_ode_check.py family
   276	A). For the one reachable M = 2 case nu = 3 (see §6):
   277	
   278	    a_{1,2} = (sigma/2)(1 ± 1/sqrt 3),  b = 2 sigma / 3,
   279	    a_1 / a_2 = 2 + sqrt 3.
   280	
   281	So the two pole-direction cubes c_i^3 = a_i have PINNED ratio 2 ± sqrt 3,
   282	and the resonant direction e (e^3 = b) is pinned to (2/3) sigma. This is
   283	simultaneously (i) the disproof of any vertex-local L1-IIa — the pattern
   284	exists — and (ii) a rigid, falsifiable prediction for any candidate
   285	counterexample pair. (At (nu, l) = (3,3), (5,3), (3,5), (5,1), (7,1) the
   286	analogous systems also have solutions over C — nonconstant determining
   287	polynomials — but none of these is reachable by the double ratio
   288	equations from row-1 chains: §6. First-step closed forms: IIa: n =
   289	((8-l)nu - 1)/(l nu + 1), n odd: exactly (nu,l,n) = (3,1,5) — the
   290	exhibit; I(nu=1): n = 8/l - 1: (1,2,3) and (1,4,1), dead by L1b; ZCH:
   291	n = ((4-l)nu + 4)/(l nu): (2,1,5) [M=1] and (2,3,1), dead by §4b.
   292	Deeper merges change nothing: every in-caps parent pair lands on the
   293	same cell list with the same unique survivor.)
   294	
   295	Suffix-side (same tier): the St 9.7/exhibit suffix shape (42,126,7,3,5)
   296	= St 9.6(iii) case (A) pattern, p = (t-A)^2 (t-B), q = eta (t-A)(t-B),
   297	nu = 7, rho = 7/5 (q-shape forced by the root law — E7 corrected form).
   298	The overdetermined coefficient system (3 residual polynomials in B after
   299	gauge A = 1) has gcd exactly (t - 3/2): unique solution B = (3/2)A, side
   300	conditions fine (family C). The distinguished chain is coefficient-
   301	consistent at BOTH its non-generic vertices, each rigid up to one scale.
   302	The pole vertices are too: p_g = ⊖ eta (eta^2 - (3/2) w_i^2) (§1). What
   303	remains unchecked is one level deeper still: the SUBSTITUTION transport
   304	between levels (only degrees + top coefficients are pinned by printed
   305	St 3.9), i.e. genuine Puiseux realizability — the same tier open for
   306	every campaign survivor, but now with every pattern datum explicit.
