    21	  B. merged nu=1, l extra simple q-roots: p = (e-a1)(e-a2), q = p*s:
    22	       E := rho*p*s' + (rho-1)*p'*s = ctilde.
    23	  C. single-pole suffix shape St 9.6(iii)(A) (mu=2, k=1, nu=7):
    24	       p = pt = (t-A)^2 (t-B), q = eta * w(t), w = (t-A)(t-B) (rad form),
    25	       E := rho*pt*w + nu*rho*t*pt*w' - nu*t*pt'*w = ctilde * pt.
    26	     Also shows the PRINTED form q = eta*(t-A)^2-type is impossible (root law).
    27	All solving is small linear algebra over Fraction after fixing the scaling.
