# Independent avenue audit after the D23 quotient reduction

Snapshot: 2026-08-19, before the stated 08:28Z cap.  Probabilities below are
my epistemic estimates, not certificate grades.  Unless a row says otherwise,
the time probability is for a focused 30-day push with the present people and
fleet.  Modular statements are over the algebraic closure of the named finite
field.

## Executive summary — five lines

1. D23 is still pending, but both current 72-variable and 29-variable objects are one specialized radical fiber, not full residue A; I put the completed representative-fiber outcome at about 85% NONEMPTY and only 5–15% on a full 36-fiber D23 kill.
2. The proposed normal-form quick shot has now been carried out exactly at `p=105337`: no row has constant NF, and the six rows collapse to two solvable auxiliary differences plus only **three independent 10-term core obstructions**.
3. The best next solver object is therefore the original 22-variable D21 fiber core plus those three rows (29 equations, 5,378 terms), not a naive 397-polynomial warm start; the latter is useful only through an explicit known-basis interface.
4. FC5 does not telescope to the Sigray mass bound: the exact natural mass potential changes with both signs on admissible merge data; moreover `sum(ab/nu)<=1` would give only the typewise bound `td<=alpha*beta`, not the absolute G5 bound.
5. The td-7/td-12 results remain honest book-tier results, td-11 still rests on FC1-R+FC3, the char-0 plan is conditional on a genuinely global kill, and the positive formal-germ/counterexample branch is not promotion-safe yet.

## 1. Probability-weighted state of every live avenue

I separate the validity of a narrow, already stated result from the chance
that it grows into the next campaign-level claim.  Timeouts are censored
runtime observations, not mathematical evidence.

