  1181	
  1182	The merged-emission law is valuable as a deterministic transition rule, but
  1183	it is not the missing global accountant. Its exact pole-mass interface is
  1184	\(\Phi_s\); that potential is nonmonotone on coefficient-solvable charts,
  1185	and FC5 can erase an arbitrarily large fixed-type scale. Depth closure and
  1186	NF-M then quotient what remains only after the unbounded entry/schema
  1187	parameters have been fixed.
  1188	
  1189	The minimum honest next theorem is not another emission identity. It is a
  1190	global Keller/proximity statement at divergence centers--KME-2 for the sharp
  1191	bound, or KME-finite for any typewise bound--together with SP to cover the
  1192	merge-blind one-pole sector. Absolute book cofinality additionally requires a
  1193	selected-counterexample type cap and full-configuration landing.
  1194	
  1195	No `td` upper bound, sharp or weak, is proved here. The new proved output is
  1196	the obstruction: **the present FC5 + depth + NF-M bookkeeping is
  1197	noncoercive, even at fixed type, and the precise missing information is the
  1198	global normalized mismatch/proximity energy.**

